{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_42","type":"agent_message","text":"The first broad call on the matched sample found only one weak region, so peak count alone is not an adequate or stable classifier here. I’m using the Galaxy UDT route for a transparent diagnostic report over the sampled tagAligns: fixed genomic-bin occupancy, concentration/entropy, signal–control enrichment, broad-run lengths, read lengths, and strand balance. This is a custom computation because no ordinary Galaxy wrapper exposes that combined set of tagAlign diagnostics; the report will remain the evidence-bearing terminal dataset."}}
